# ---- Counted nouns ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Slovenian plural rule (assets/i18n): one (1, 101, 201 ...) | two (2, 102 ...) | few (3, 4, 103, 104
# ...) | other (0, 5-100, and 21, 22, 23 ...: "enaindvajset potez"). The noun follows the dual after
# 2: "dve potezi", "dva kmeta". The base key is the nominative; every noun also has:
#   _acc   accusative ("Beli je naredil {n:mistake_acc}." = "eno napako / dve napaki / pet napak";
#          "pridobiš {pts:point_acc}"); the masculine animate ones (kmet, napadalec, branilec): "enega
#          kmeta, dva kmeta, tri kmete, pet kmetov"
#   _gen   genitive (after do, od, brez, blizu, a negation: "brez {n:mistake_gen}" = "brez ene napake /
#          dveh napak / petih napak")
#   _loc   locative (after v, na, o, pri: "mat v {m:move_loc}" = "mat v eni potezi / dveh potezah /
#          petih potezah", the Slovenian "mate in N")
# There is no dative or instrumental ("z dvema napakama", "s tremi"): rephrase ("imaš dve napaki in eno
# grobo napako", or a list after a colon). The written forms show the digits ("v 3 potezah"). The
# _gen / _loc keys are for counts of 1 or more (0 would be said "ničih").
# "figura" counts every chessman, pawns included.
count.move = {n:f} poteza|{n:f} potezi|{n:f} poteze|{n} potez
